# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to comit the .python-version file.
#   For an app, you may want to ignore it.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1173, it is a good idea to include Pipfile.lock in git.
#   But if you don't want to, uncomment the following line:
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Poetry uses poetry.lock to ensure reproducible builds. It's recommended to commit it.
#   But if you prefer to ignore it, uncomment the following line:
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   PDM stores project-wide configurations in .pdm.toml
.pdm.toml
.pdm-plugins/
.pdm-build/

